# Sentinel-developed features use real-locus tests

When a feature or filter is designed from named sentinels (gold-review ranks,
nssv/catalog IDs, IGV loci, chr22/1KG overlap sites), tests for that feature
must load `tests/fixtures/loci/<id>/`. Replace cartoon tests with those
fixtures. Do not keep a parallel hand-built DataFrame of clips and DPE.

This applies while writing the feature (`src/`, scripts) and the tests, not
only when a test file is already open.

## Required

- Extract with `scripts/extract_locus_fixture.py` (BAM snippet + extract tables).
- Run the real function on those tables (`_assign_gold_stage`, picker, etc.).
- Assert the catalog breakpoint or the keep/drop the sentinel was meant to show.
- Assert the BAM still contains a read named in `supporting_reads_detail.mei.tsv`.
- Replay the old bug on the fixture before calling the test done.

## Do not

- Invent 4 clips and 17 DPE for a named site or for a rule taken from one.
- Treat “this is just a scoring rule” as permission to skip extraction.
- Ship cartoon tests that pass while the real sentinel still fails.

Follow `.cursor/skills/real-locus-test-fixtures/SKILL.md`.
